  "result": "Fixed. A child `Context` now takes its own section of the parent's `default_map`, keyed by `info_name`, so `default_map={'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` now prints `changed`. Before, the child received the parent's whole map and never found its own keys. The change is one line in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`: `parent.default_map.get(info_name)` replaces `parent.default_map`.\n\nI added `test_group_default_map_applies_to_subcommand` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It checks that the `default_map` value is used and that the option falls back to `normal` when no map is given. The verification command `python -m pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_defaults.py -q` gives 145 passed.\n\nI didn't run the rest of the test suite.",
